propresenter-bundle includes work by others, under their own licences.

1. The ProPresenter schema

   proto/ is the community schema from https://github.com/greyshirtguy/ProPresenter7-Proto, its
   "autogen-proto" folder (generated from ProPresenter 21.4; proto/version.txt), copied without
   change. MIT licence, Copyright (c) 2023 greyshirtguy; the full text is in proto/LICENSE.

   src/proto.json is that schema compiled by scripts/compile-schema.js, with one change of this
   package's own: rv.data.Graphics.Text.Attributes.CustomAttribute field 12, which the schema names
   original_font, is kept as _unknown_12 (repeated raw bytes), the form this package reads and
   writes each run of text's font in. The bytes in a file are the same either way. That change is
   this package's own, under its MIT licence (LICENSE).

2. Format research by others

   While the file format was being worked out, earlier versions of this work consulted these
   projects. A comparison of their code with this package's found nothing copied (the only shared
   text is ProPresenter's own RTF header and the schema's field names). They are named here as
   credit:
     - https://github.com/davbeck/pro-crud (MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 David Beck)
     - https://github.com/rainman80s/propresenter-claude-skill (MIT)
     - https://github.com/cgarwood/propresenter-presentation-builder

3. Google's protobuf types

   src/proto.json also contains Google's standard protobuf types (google.protobuf: the
   descriptor and wrapper types the schema imports), compiled from the copies in proto/google,
   which came with the upstream schema without their comments. Google's licence for them:

